    "timeline_JgHEJa": {
      "type": "timeline",
      "blocks": {
        "item_WKdnhc": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/1_2b0e277e-9650-4f8e-8b7d-13b943a9c162.png",
            "label": "history",
            "subheading": "",
            "title": "<strong>From power to Promise</strong>",
            "content": "<p><strong>Because the pinky has always meant something.</strong></p><p><strong>For centuries, signet rings were worn as symbols of identity, family, status and power.</strong></p><p><strong>Kings, politicians and people of influence wore them on their little finger A tiny ring that said:</strong></p><p><strong>This is who I am.</strong></p><p><strong>We loved that.</strong></p><p><strong>But instead of wearing somebody else's history, we wanted to create jewellery that could hold your own.</strong></p>",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_style": "link",
            "mobile_text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "item_PjAGM6": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/2_8ccb730e-45a9-4d05-b024-4072334b8831.png",
            "label": "REINVENTED",
            "subheading": "",
            "title": "<strong>&nbsp;THE PROMISE RING, REINVENTED&nbsp;</strong>",
            "content": "<p><strong>Promise rings have existed in different forms for hundreds of years.</strong></p><p><strong>But somewhere along the way, the promise ring became defined almost entirely by romantic relationships - often as the ring before </strong><em><strong>the</strong></em><strong> ring.</strong></p><p><em><strong>We wanted to change that.</strong></em></p><p><strong>When we created The Promise Co., we built a new world around what a promise could mean.</strong></p><p><strong>A promise to your partner, to your best friend, to your family.</strong></p><p><strong>And, perhaps most importantly, a promise to yourself.</strong></p>",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_style": "link",
            "mobile_text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "item_qwAGtH": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/5_3fcf85bf-43d1-4056-bc38-993d1905bcca.png",
            "label": "why pinky?",
            "subheading": "",
            "title": "<strong>todays modern promise</strong>",
            "content": "<p><strong>The smallest finger has always carried more weight than you might expect.</strong></p><p><strong>Historically the home of the signet ring - a piece designed to represent exactly who its wearer was - the pinky feels like the natural home for a modern promise.</strong></p><p><strong>Not a placeholder for an engagement.</strong></p><p><strong>Not something defined by anybody else.</strong></p><p><strong>Something chosen by you, for whatever matters to you.</strong></p><p><strong>Your finger. Your story. Your promise.</strong></p>",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_url": "",
            "link_style": "link",
            "mobile_text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        }
      },
